# The gate-first list: the paths whose change keeps EVERY gate before the merge (cc-land, ordinary). Every other
# PR is ordinary and lands optimistically — on its worker's own green and the static gates, its suite run once on
# the base after the batch it merged with, and reverted out loud if that goes red. Owner, 2026-09-24: "protected
# paths (cc-guard, cc-sandbox, cc-land itself, hooks, anything security) keep the full gate before merge".
# One path or glob per line, relative to the tree this file describes (bin/…, not core/bin/…). Read from the BASE
# side of a diff, so a PR cannot take itself off this list. A repo that ships no such list lands nothing
# optimistically. The box's own protected paths (CC_PROTECTED_PATHS_<repo>) hold as well, and outrank this.

# the landing itself, and the two lists it reads at the base
bin/cc-land
tests/gate-first
tests/control-layer
tests/green.sh

# the guard, the sandbox and the boundary
bin/cc-guard
bin/cc-sandbox
bin/ccbox
ccbox/*

# hooks: what runs unattended on every commit and every tool call
.githooks/*

# secrets, tokens, permissions and what widens them
bin/cc-gh-token
bin/cc-trust
bin/cc-config
bin/cc-settings
bin/cc-scope
bin/cc-github-deny
install.sh
